    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-pairs\n\n### Description\n\nHi, firstly thank you for your excellent plugin suite!\r\n\r\nI was wondering how to configure the following two scenarios with mini-pairs:\r\n\r\n1. Single backtick should place the cursor in the middle and close with a single pairing backtick. (Example: writing a single line code block in markdown)\r\n2. Triple backticks should place the cursor after the third backtick and close with triple pairing backticks (Example:  writing multi-line code blocks in a markdown file).\r\n\r\nAny suggestions?",
