            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": ">     1. Single backtick should place the cursor in the middle and close with a single pairing backtick. (Example: writing a single line code block in markdown)\r\n\r\nIf I understand you correctly, it is already a default behavior: typing `` ` `` in empty line will lead to `` `|` `` (`|` meaning cursor).\r\n\r\n>     2. Triple backticks should place the cursor after the third backtick and close with triple pairing backticks (Example:  writing multi-line code blocks in a markdown file).\r\n\r\n`mini.pairs` is designed to work only with single previous and single next characters. This was done to make functionality as fast as possible. Working with a greater number of previous/next symbols should be done with snippets, in my opinion.\r\n\r\nDoes it answer you question?",
